THOUGHT: `instructions` is annotated @Nullable and explicitly set to null in `unload()`, while `getInstructions()` has no nullability annotation but is treated as @NonNull by NullAway. Other similar accessors (e.g., `getArgRegs()`) throw if data is not initialized instead of returning null. To satisfy NullAway and keep behavior consistent, I should make `getInstructions()` throw a `JadxRuntimeException` when `instructions` is null, and annotate it as `@NotNull`. This avoids changing the field’s lifecycle and should not introduce new errors. After editing, I’ll run the compile task to confirm the NullAway error count drops by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '300,312s/public InsnNode\[\] getInstructions() {/	@NotNull
	public InsnNode[] getInstructions() {
		if (instructions == null) {
			throw new JadxRuntimeException("Method instructions not loaded: " + this
					+ ", class status: " + parentClass.getTopParentClass().getState());
		}/' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/nodes/MethodNode.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

